Tesla will set aside its AI5 chip exclusively for the Optimus robot, a product that CEO Elon Musk said he believes will one day be the biggest in the world. The decision sparked conversation regarding AI4’s prowess and capability as a self-driving chip, and less-than-fond memories of the Hardware 3 conundrum that many owners find themselves in to this day.

Musk stated on November 22 that Tesla vehicles will remain on the AI4 computer, which he said it sufficient to achieve “superhuman driving,” while the next generation AI5 chip will be set aside for Optimus . Musk was initially asked by a Hardware 3 Model Y owner when AI5 would appear in new cars.

